error[NK2115]: `async` stands before a `let`, but `async` is a prefix of an expression.
  --> tests/async_parse_before_a_let_is_refused.nika:5:2
   |
 5 | 	async let x = 1
   |  ^^^^^
   |
   = note: It starts a task where a value is computed, so it stands on the right of the `=`.
   = help: Write it before the value: `let x = async f()`.
